  "existing_issue": {
    "body": "# Distinguish reviewed native molecular alternatives from product identity in candidate checks\n\nThe isolated #1241 candidate's real second-cycle export passed byte-for-byte,\nbut `consumer-review-02` failed its synonym assertion: the acceptance helper\nrequires all four explicit structural names to return CHEBI:86658. One exact\nspelling selects CHEBI:196822 from an earlier, unchanged native-xref row.\nPreserve this failed receipt; it is not completed consumer acceptance.\n\nIndependent extraction from pinned raw ChEBI\n`a5d40380ab78bde0e8b5a704dbee3cba2bcaa7608be46eebc2f4a92932516c9b`\nshows both IDs have identical full InChI, InChIKey, stereospecific SMILES,\nformula and charge 0. The extractor retained their complete declarations and\nincident assertions, not formula-only or lexical evidence. All 19 mapping rows\ntargeting CHEBI:196822 or CHEBI:16110 are unchanged from the baseline candidate.\n\nSeparately, generic L-alpha/L-alpha-symbol queries select CHEBI:16110 only with\nsynonyms enabled. This is an unchanged native related-synonym route to a +1\nwildcard-R class, not exact structural identity or supplier P3556 identity.\nThe explicit P3556 source guard must continue retaining the original local\ningredient. No runtime precedence change, global identifier merge, new same_as\nassertion, native synonym removal or new product grounding is authorized.\n\nFix the finite acceptance check: bind the retained native/full-row witnesses,\nallow CHEBI:196822 only for the exact reviewed structural spelling, distinguish\nthe two reviewed generic lexical-class outcomes, and require review for any\nnew alternative. Preserve canonical-label, native alias availability, removed\nMIM exact-xref, chloride, parent, Potato and unrelated positive controls.\nCheck actual final-candidate rows against the retained complete competing rows.\nTest altered structures/charges, other spellings/targets, missing evidence,\nchanged candidate rows/multiplicity, and canonical-mode misuse. Run replacement\nacceptance only in a new attempt after independent review; keep old helper and\nfailed receipts unchanged.\n\nEvidence: `identity-candidate-1241.7Zc6Ur/reader-diagnostic-1247.ZQSqrf/`\n`NATIVE-INTERPRETATION.md`; `native-alternative-authority.json` SHA-256\n`1cee9914ee50e7e2b7af2598df14339943130ad26684117562bb0c2dfb6491e8`.\nThis is an external acceptance-helper defect, not proof of a new chemical\nmapping regression. Final source replay and all-source KG acceptance remain pending.\n",
